KBV_DOC1 :: "---\nid: statistics.mmd-estimators\nversion: 1\nkind: method\ntitle: Biased and unbiased MMD estimators\nstatus: admitted\n---\n## Details\nThe unbiased estimator divides the within-sample sums by m^2.\n";
KBV_DOC1_SHA :: "19952efa5bd4a152bec6f05fb32966c874f877c62075df3592e246447c600277";
KBV_TEXT_A :: "---\nid: statistics.mmd-estimators\nversion: 1\nkind: method\ntitle: Biased and unbiased MMD estimators\nstatus: admitted\n---\n## Details\nThe unbiased estimator divides the within-sample sums by m(m-1).\n";
KBV_TEXT_A_SHA :: "b36739956f4d7586d0fbc833d438b2bcd60057976fbc9f831ca3c60ddcd5d0e8";
KBV_TEXT_B :: "---\nid: statistics.mmd-estimators\nversion: 1\nkind: method\ntitle: Biased and unbiased MMD estimators\nstatus: admitted\n---\n## Details\nThe unbiased estimator divides the within-sample sums by m^2.\n## How to check\nTwo samples from one distribution give an unbiased value near 0.\n";
KBV_TEXT_B_SHA :: "f6b5ef98863f56a99673b94dbb55162fd1fa8bc8f9e0e2f53b6d4e004c80db3b";
KBV_DOC2 :: "---\nid: statistics.mmd-estimators\nversion: 2\nkind: method\ntitle: Biased and unbiased MMD estimators\nstatus: admitted\n---\n## Details\nThe unbiased estimator divides the within-sample sums by m(m-1).\n## How to check\nTwo samples from one distribution give an unbiased value near 0.\n";
